IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-3-punishments`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 14 -- Public tranquility`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 267A, 267B, 267C, 268, 268A, 268B, 268C, 290, 291.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The first of three modules for Chapter 14. This one holds the public-order
-- sections: AFFRAY (s 267A, punished by s 267B), INCITEMENT to violence or
-- disobedience (s 267C), PUBLIC NUISANCE (s 268, punished by s 290, continued after
-- an injunction by s 291), and the three HOAX sections -- communicating false
-- information of a harmful thing (s 268A), placing or sending a thing intending to
-- cause fear of harm (s 268B), and placing or sending one knowing of the real risk
-- of that fear (s 268C).
--
-- ss 268A to 268C are items 1 and 2 of the Schedule to s 4B, so with this module the
-- s 4B classifier in agent-compliance.l4 is computed for every item but the open
-- item 15.
--
-- s 267C has two shapes with the same content and fault. s 267C(1) is UTTERING or
-- PUBLISHING the inciting matter, intending or knowing it likely that violence,
-- disobedience or breach of the peace will occur as a result. s 267C(2) is MAKING
-- or POSSESSING it for the purpose of publishing, with the same intent or knowledge
-- as to what the carrying out of that purpose will produce. s 267C(4) widens
-- "counselling disobedience" to instruction, advice or information that promotes it;
-- the content fact carries that width.
--
-- s 268's Explanation -- a common nuisance is not excused by the convenience or
-- advantage it also brings -- is encoded by conjoining nothing about advantage.
--
-- ss 267B and 290 are punishment sections and are computed here. s 290 also creates
-- the offence of public nuisance "in any case not otherwise punishable by this
-- Code", so it has a constitutive rule too; and s 291 is a distinct offence on the
-- continuance.

§§ `Sections 267A and 267B -- Affray`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 267A"
@export Decide whether the person commits an affray under Penal Code 1871 section 267A
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Two or more persons disturbing the public peace by fighting in a public place, the person being one of them.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an affray` IF
    pn's `two or more persons disturb the public peace by fighting in a public place and the person is one of them`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 267B"
@export Give the punishment for committing an affray under Penal Code 1871 section 267B
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for affray` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine up to or both` 1 5000

§§ `Section 267C -- Incitement to violence or disobedience`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 267C(1)"
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person publishes inciting matter within section 267C(1)` IF
        pn's `utters words or makes a sign or visible representation or places before a person an object or posts publishes distributes sells or offers for sale a document or communicates an electronic record`
    AND pn's `the words sign representation object document or electronic record contains an incitement to violence or counsels disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant or is likely to lead to a breach of the peace`
    AND (   pn's `intends violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace to occur`
         OR pn's `knows or has reason to believe that violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace is likely to occur as a result`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 267C(2)"
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person makes or possesses inciting matter for publication within section 267C(2)` IF
        pn's `makes prints or otherwise reproduces imports possesses or has under his control such a document for the purpose of posting publishing distributing selling or offering it for sale or makes such an electronic record for the purpose of communicating it`
    AND pn's `the words sign representation object document or electronic record contains an incitement to violence or counsels disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant or is likely to lead to a breach of the peace`
    AND (   pn's `intends violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace to occur by the carrying out of that purpose`
         OR pn's `knows or has reason to believe that violence disobedience to the law or such lawful order or breach of the peace is likely to occur by the carrying out of that purpose`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 267C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes uttering words or making or publishing a document containing incitement to violence or disobedience under Penal Code 1871 section 267C
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Uttering, publishing or communicating matter containing an incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or a lawful order, or likely to lead to a breach of the peace, intending or knowing it likely that such a result will follow; or making or possessing such matter for publication with the same intent or knowledge as to what publication will produce.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes incitement to violence or disobedience` IF
        `the person publishes inciting matter within section 267C(1)` pn
    OR  `the person makes or possesses inciting matter for publication within section 267C(2)` pn

§§ `Section 268 -- Public nuisance`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 268"
@export Decide whether the person is guilty of a public nuisance under Penal Code 1871 section 268
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc An act or illegal omission which causes common injury, danger or annoyance to the public or to the people who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity, or which must necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may use a public right. Convenience or advantage is no excuse.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of a public nuisance` IF
        pn's `does an act or is guilty of an illegal omission`
    AND (   pn's `the act or omission causes common injury danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity`
         OR pn's `the act or omission must necessarily cause injury obstruction danger or annoyance to persons who may have occasion to use a public right`)

§§ `Sections 268A to 268C -- False information and things causing fear of harm`

-- s 268A is the hoax by words: communicating information that refers to the presence
-- of a harmful thing somewhere, knowing the reference to be false or fabricated.
-- ss 268B and 268C are the hoax by object, sharing the placing or sending and the
-- absence of reasonable excuse, and differing in fault: s 268B intends to induce the
-- belief that the thing is harmful; s 268C acts intentionally knowing there is a
-- real risk that persons would so believe. Neither needs a particular person in
-- mind (ss 268B(2), 268C(2)), which is encoded by conjoining nothing about one.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 268A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes communicating false information of a harmful thing under Penal Code 1871 section 268A
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Transmitting or communicating, or causing to be, information referring to the presence of a thing likely to cause hurt or property damage in a place or conveyance, knowing the reference to be false or fabricated.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes communicating false information of a harmful thing` IF
        pn's `transmits or communicates or causes to be transmitted or communicated information which contains a reference to the presence in any place or location or in any conveyance or means of transportation of a thing that is likely to cause hurt or damage to property by any means`
    AND pn's `knows that the reference is false or fabricated`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 268B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes placing or sending a thing with intent to cause fear of harm under Penal Code 1871 section 268B
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Without reasonable excuse, placing a thing in a place or conveyance or sending it by post, courier or other means, intending to induce in others a belief that it is likely to cause hurt or property damage.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes placing or sending a thing with intent to cause fear of harm` IF
        pn's `places a thing in any place or location or in any conveyance or means of transportation or sends a thing from one place to another by post courier or any other means`
    AND NOT pn's `has a reasonable excuse`
    AND pn's `intends to induce in one or more other persons a belief that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property by any means`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 268C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes placing or sending a thing causing fear of harm under Penal Code 1871 section 268C
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Intentionally and without reasonable excuse, placing or sending a thing knowing there is a real risk that others would believe it likely to cause hurt or property damage.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes placing or sending a thing causing fear of harm` IF
        pn's `places a thing in any place or location or in any conveyance or means of transportation or sends a thing from one place to another by post courier or any other means`
    AND pn's `places or sends the thing intentionally`
    AND NOT pn's `has a reasonable excuse`
    AND pn's `knows that there is a real risk that one or more persons would believe that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property by any means`

§§ `Sections 290 and 291 -- Punishment for public nuisance, and its continuance`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 290"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes the offence of public nuisance under Penal Code 1871 section 290
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc A s 268 public nuisance in a case not otherwise punishable by this Code.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes the offence of public nuisance` IF
        `the person is guilty of a public nuisance` pn
    AND NOT pn's `the public nuisance is otherwise punishable by this Code`

-- (a) fine up to $2,000; (b) where the offender knew the act or omission would or
-- would probably cause the common injury, danger or annoyance, up to 3 months or
-- $2,000 or both; (c) the same on a second or subsequent conviction.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 290"
@export Give the punishment for public nuisance under Penal Code 1871 section 290
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc The nuisance facts. Fine up to $2,000, or up to 3 months imprisonment as well where the offender knew the nuisance would or would probably result, or on a second or subsequent conviction.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for public nuisance` pn IS
    IF      pn's `knew that the act or omission constituting the public nuisance will cause or will probably cause common injury danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity`
        OR  pn's `this is a second or subsequent conviction`
    THEN `imprisonment up to or fine up to or both` (3 DIVIDED BY 12) 2000
    ELSE `fine up to only` 2000

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 291"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes continuing a public nuisance after an injunction to discontinue under Penal Code 1871 section 291
GIVEN pn IS A `Public Nuisance` @desc Repeating or continuing a public nuisance after being enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority not to.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes continuing a public nuisance after an injunction` IF
        pn's `repeats or continues a public nuisance`
    AND pn's `has been enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority to issue such an injunction not to repeat or continue the nuisance`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes affray or incitement` IF
        (   `the person commits an affray` (a's `public nuisance`)
         OR `constitutes incitement to violence or disobedience` (a's `public nuisance`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes public nuisance` IF
        (   `constitutes the offence of public nuisance` (a's `public nuisance`)
         OR `constitutes continuing a public nuisance after an injunction` (a's `public nuisance`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a hoax of a harmful thing` IF
        (   `constitutes communicating false information of a harmful thing` (a's `public nuisance`)
         OR `constitutes placing or sending a thing with intent to cause fear of harm` (a's `public nuisance`)
         OR `constitutes placing or sending a thing causing fear of harm` (a's `public nuisance`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
